      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"5\">Level 5 - Interview-ready</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Graphs</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>MST, Bridges and Euler Paths</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Three graph questions that sound alike and are not: \"connect everything as cheaply as possible\" (minimum spanning tree), \"which single link would split the network\" (bridges and cut vertices), and \"use every edge exactly once\" (Euler paths). This page builds each one from a picture to a tested template, with the variants Google-style SDE-3 rounds like to add: virtual vertices, critical edges, offline minimax queries and the dead-end trap in Reconstruct Itinerary.</p>\n"
